# `results/*.json` ignores scratch harness output. Every file that is evidence
# is un-ignored by name below, so a tracked result is a declared one rather
# than a historical `git add -f` nobody can see. S4/S5 predate this comment and
# are tracked already; they are listed so the set is readable in one place.
!results/S2-executed.json
!results/S4-executed.json
!results/S5-executed.json
!results/S2-toolchoice-2026-10-04.json
